F. Procedure
The duration of the experiment was 75 minutes. After the welcoming, participants had to read and sign the safety instruction and declaration of consent. Afterwards, participants had to ﬁll out the demographic questionnaire. Participants were instructed in written form for reasons of standardization about the driving simulator, the capabilities of the partially ADS, the possibility of malfunctions and, depending on the ARHUD or Baseline condition, about the HMI concept. After entering the vehicle and adjusting the mirrors and seat, an 8-minute familiarization drive took place. During the familiarization drive, participants had to drive manually and then experienced an automated drive with two request to intervene scenarios by using the Baseline concept. A malfunction did not occur during the familiarization drive. Then the eye-tracking system was calibrated and the 27-minute experimental drive was started. Each take-over during the experimental drive was followed by an intermediate survey. After the experimental drive, a follow-up questionnaire was conducted. The experiment was concluded with payment of a compensation of 10 e.

